# =============================================================================
# What this repository publishes
# =============================================================================
# This working tree is the full research workspace for the MAGICC study. The
# PUBLIC repository is deliberately a strict subset: the installable package,
# its tests, the reproduction workflow, the container and conda specifications,
# the frozen V5 model, and the small artefacts those three need in order to
# work from a clean clone.
#
# Everything else -- manuscripts, reviewer material, private notes, raw and
# derived data, training checkpoints, analysis scripts, logs -- is excluded
# here and belongs either in the data repository, at figshare, or nowhere
# public at all.
# =============================================================================

# --- Python build and cache artefacts ----------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
/dist/
/build/

# --- Manuscript, reviewer and private material: NEVER publish ----------------
manuscript/
manuscript2/
manuscript3/
nature_communications/
project_design_and_protocol*.md
project_progress_and_results*.md
supervisor*.md
info.txt
*.docx

# --- Data ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The benchmark genomes, splits and per-sample metadata are distributed through
# the data repository (https://github.com/renmaotian/magicc-data) and figshare,
# not here. The two files re-included below are the k-mer list and the
# normalisation parameters that docker/Dockerfile bakes into the image; they
# are small and the container build fails without them.
data/*
!data/features/
data/features/*
!data/features/normalization_params.json
!data/kmer_selection/
data/kmer_selection/*
!data/kmer_selection/selected_kmers.txt
!data/kmer_selection/selected_kmers_annotated.tsv

# --- Results ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Result files are deposited at figshare. Re-included below: the model card
# (the container build verifies the bundled model against it), the recorded
# metrics table that workflow/ checks its reproduction against, and the
# determinism statement that README.md links to.
results/*
!results/revision/
results/revision/*
!results/revision/model_card.json
!results/revision/metrics/
results/revision/metrics/*
!results/revision/metrics/ws5.5_table_S2_rebuilt.tsv
!results/revision/reproducibility/
results/revision/reproducibility/*
!results/revision/reproducibility/DETERMINISM.md
!results/revision/reproducibility/determinism_report.json

# --- Analysis code, third-party tools, logs, run state ------------------------
# The analysis scripts are released separately (see Code availability).
/scripts/
/tools/
/logs/
.snakemake/

# --- Large reference inputs to the training pipeline --------------------------
85_bcg.hmm
uacg.hmm

# --- Models -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Only the frozen, released V5 ONNX artefact is published (via Git LFS).
# PyTorch checkpoints, superseded ONNX versions, training curves/logs and the
# two taxonomic-holdout models are excluded: together they are ~65 GB, and the
# holdout weights belong with the holdout evaluation files at figshare.
models/*
!models/magicc_v5.onnx

# --- Built container images (rebuild with containers/build_containers.sh) -----
# The definition files docker/Dockerfile and containers/magicc.def ARE tracked.
containers/*.sif
containers/*.tar

# --- Temp files ----------------------------------------------------------------
temp_download_*.zip
